Original commit body from a14342690caebbb4e1a1ed2d66ead4967b7b8ea0:

c.py stamped an unresolved ambiguous libc call (send, recv, read, ...)
with the file's ANGLE includes only. The coverage gate's ALL-expansion
(INV-zimud) reads that stamp as the complete set of the call's homes,
so a header reached through a quoted include or transitively was a
false all-clear: `#include <errno.h>` + `#include "net.h"` (which
includes <sys/socket.h>) stamped a real send() as errno.h, and
NO-NET-SEND read CONFIRMED with no caveat.

New include_closure.IncludeClosure: one include graph per run. The
stamp is every header the file includes, quoted or angled, plus
everything a header found in the repository includes, breadth-first,
each named as written. An unfound / unread / past-depth header keeps
its name (never nothing); several repository candidates are all read
(every resolution error only ADDS a header). c.py uses it for the stamp
and for WI-rimon's included-header test.

